 "snp.intro": {
  "text": "A ZFS snapshot freezes a dataset as it is: it costs almost no space at first and grows only with the changes. A daily one before the container updates lets you bring back any container's data from the last days. The whole dataset is never rolled back; a single container can be restored, with a safety snapshot first.",
  "note": "lead line at the top of the Snapshots page (Settings, Utilities, Snapshots). \"safety snapshot\" is a snapshot of now, made before a restore."
 },
